35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The minute books show the lower grade stopped nominating. The rota confirms the same nine people handle setup and lock-up.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, nine people carrying the load is a recipe for burnout. My data shows chasing individual payments takes six hours monthly, versus one for yearly collections.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, that aligns with my findings. The same nine people do the setup and lock-up, while eighteen members never sign in. The burden is incredibly uneven.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, eighteen ghosts? That explains the hesitation. My data shows eleven mid-year joiners needed hand-worked calculations, and nine tasters refused a whole-year commitment.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, six hours chasing payments is unacceptable. My ledger shows fixed costs are seventy percent, but the bank statements prove a third of renewals need reminders. We cannot guess the income.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, the taster refusal confirms the barrier is visibility. If the structure is opaque, newcomers drift away. We need a model that preserves that anonymity.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, anonymity is a luxury we cannot afford if the books are a mess. I need a system that minimizes the chasing, not just the visibility.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I understand the need for order. But if the fee structure feels like a trap, those eighteen will stay silent. We need clarity, not just collection.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Benjamin, clarity is the point. If the fee feels like a trap, people vanish. I need a structure that makes the commitment obvious, not a maze of calculations.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Shunichi, I agree. If the fee feels like a trap, people vanish. I need a structure that makes the commitment obvious, not a maze of calculations.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, I agree. We need a flat, predictable cost. No itemized ledgers that expose individual spending. That preserves the anonymity that keeps people comfortable here.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, a flat fee is logical, but only if it covers the fixed costs without requiring me to chase stragglers. I need the collection to be automatic, not a personal favor.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Asuka, I agree. A flat fee protects the quiet members from scrutiny. But we must ensure the nine who carry the work are not overburdened by the collection process itself.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Asuka, I agree. A flat fee removes the anxiety of the unknown. If the cost is clear, the hesitation to show up disappears.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"@Asuka, a flat fee is the only way to stop the guessing. But if a third of people need reminders, how do we ensure the money actually arrives on time?","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, automatic direct debit solves the reminder problem. It removes the social friction of chasing people, which is exactly what I want to avoid.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, direct debit is elegant, but it requires a clean, one-time setup. I need to ensure the initial data entry doesn’t become a new administrative nightmare for the next treasurer.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I agree. A one-time setup is manageable if we document it clearly. I would rather spend a few hours now than chase payments for a year.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Benjamin, a one-time setup is fine. The real win is that the fee is fixed and known. No more wondering if the cost will change.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"@Benjamin, I agree. A one-time setup is better than a year of chasing. But I need the numbers to prove the flat fee covers the fixed costs without a deficit.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
